+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional ``canonical`` option gives the type
+   represented by the alias. It is shown after the alias name, following an
+   equals sign, and parsed as a type annotation so referenced types can be
+   cross-referenced. A description body may also be provided.
+
+   Type aliases may be declared at module level or inside a class. The
+   :rst:role:`py:type` role references a declared type alias.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      The represented type, shown in the directive signature. If omitted, the
+      alias name is still documented and can be referenced.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined. The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
